%N A227724 T(n,k) = number of small equivalence classes of half full n-ary Boolean functions that contain 2^k functions.
%C A227724 Like A227725, but counting only small equivalence classes (sec) of half full Boolean functions, i.e. those with an equal number of zeros and ones.
%H A227724 Tilman Piesk, <a href="https://en.wikiversity.org/wiki/3-ary_Boolean_functions;_balanced_families">3-ary Boolean functions; balanced families</a>, Example for row 3.
%H A227724 Tilman Piesk, <a href="https://en.wikiversity.org/wiki/Properties_of_Boolean_functions#sec">Properties of Boolean functions</a>, Small equivalence classes of Boolean functions.
%H A227724 <a href="/index/Bo#Boolean">Index entries for sequences related to Boolean functions</a>
%F A227724 T(n,k) = 2^(-k)*[n k]_2*Sum_{j=0..k-1} (-1)^j*2^(j*(j-1)/2)*[k j]_2*binomial(2^(k-j),2^(k-j-1)), for 1 <= k <= n, where [n k]_2 is the Gaussian binomial coefficient with q = 2. - _Vladeta Jovovic_, Sep 28 2026
